		<h>Conclusions</h>
		<ol>
			<li>The property title of Furnace Farm House was entered onto by agents of FF.</li>
			<li>Works were done to undertake regular maintenance to the North and Eastern hedges surrounding the property where large growths had grown over and through the boundary fence.</li>
			<li>Had the works not been done there would have been an increased chance of damage being caused to {{ FFH }} caused by the proximity of the mature hawthorn hedging haws and the leading of FFS. And due to the general nature of the leaning branches being a cause of access to the building for squirrels and other rodents.</li>
			<li>some of the cuttings were left on the property of {{ FFH }} for a short but exact period unknown before being relocated onto FF as evidenced by figure n.1 (the top photo on the A4 page labelled n) provided by NHS investments notice of intent to claim.</li>
			<li>
				It is claimed and corroborated by figure n.2 provided by NHS ice of intent to claim that some cuttings were left on the access to {{ FFH }} on the track that forms a part of the title of FF but over which {{ FFH }} has a right of way.
				<ul>
					<li>agents of FF have no recollection of leaving cuttings in this location.</li>
					<li>The cutting identified in figure n.2 were removed by agents of FF once they had come to their attention.</li>
					<li>cuttings were relatively light and could easily have been moved by hand with minimal effort in order to gain access to {{ FFH }} by light vehicle.</li>
					<li>cuttings were sufficiently small as to have been no obstruction for large vehicles to drive over.</li>
